<title>ITALY: Stet names advisers on share swap.</title>
<headline>Stet names advisers on share swap.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The board of state telecom group Stet said on Thursday it has asked JP Morgan and Giubergia Warburg to evaluate Stet and Telecom Italia and recommend the appropriate share swap ratio.</p>
<p>Stet said in a statement that Telecom Italia would appoint its own advisers. Stet and Telecom are to merge ahead of the group's planned privatisation.</p>
<p>Price Waterhouse has been asked to arbitrate in the event that the two companies' respective advisers fail to agree on share swap terms.</p>
</text>
